To achieve the goal of adding test listener support to the Google Test framework, we will extend the test event listener functionality. This involves creating a new listener that can capture events during test execution and optionally integrating it into the existing testing framework.

### Step-by-Step Implementation

1. **Define a new Test Listener**: Create a test listener that records events and their details during test execution.
2. **Integrate with the existing system**: Ensure that this new listener can be added to the testing framework and easily accessed during tests.

### Implementation Code

Below, you'll find an implementation of a new listener called `CustomTestListener`, which retains information about each test's execution events. 

#### New Listener Class

We'll place this class in `googletest/test/googletest-listener-test.cc`.

```cpp
namespace internal {

class CustomTestListener : public TestEventListener {
 public:
  CustomTestListener() {}

 protected:
  void OnTestProgramStart(const UnitTest& /*unit_test*/) override {
    g_events->push_back("CustomTestListener: OnTestProgramStart");
  }

  void OnTestIterationStart(const UnitTest& /*unit_test*/, int iteration) override {
    g_events->push_back("CustomTestListener: OnTestIterationStart(" + std::to_string(iteration) + ")");
  }

  void OnTestStart(const TestInfo& test_info) override {
    g_events->push_back("CustomTestListener: OnTestStart: " + std::string(test_info.test_suite_name()) + "." + test_info.name());
  }

  void OnTestEnd(const TestInfo& test_info) override {
    g_events->push_back("CustomTestListener: OnTestEnd: " + std::string(test_info.test_suite_name()) + "." + test_info.name());
  }

  void OnTestIterationEnd(const UnitTest& /*unit_test*/, int iteration) override {
    g_events->push_back("CustomTestListener: OnTestIterationEnd(" + std::to_string(iteration) + ")");
  }

  void OnTestProgramEnd(const UnitTest& /*unit_test*/) override {
    g_events->push_back("CustomTestListener: OnTestProgramEnd");
  }

  // Add other overrides as needed...
};

}  // namespace internal
```

#### Registering the Listener

Next, we will need to modify the test runner to register `CustomTestListener`. This is typically done in the main function where the test runner is initialized, like so:

```cpp
int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  ::testing::InitGoogleTest(&argc, argv);

  // Add CustomTestListener
  testing::UnitTest::GetInstance()->listeners().Append(new internal::CustomTestListener());

  return RUN_ALL_TESTS();
}
```

### Testing the New Listener

You can now create a test that utilizes this listener to verify its functionality. Here’s a simple test case included in `googletest/test/gtest_unittest.cc`:

```cpp
